\Q\ You have just spent the night adding more online games to the BBS.
Everything seems to work, so you open the board. Do you:
\A\ Play the games and test them out
\A\ Leave them alone, and hope everything works
\A\ Wait until someone calls and hope that they test the games
\A\ Go to sleep
\N\ You play the games, and take up all the time on the BBS. No one can call,
and everyone loses interest in calling your BBS.
\N\ Someone calls, and decides to play the new games, but you haven't done 
all the work needed, and the BBS crashes (with a loud thump), creating 
another 4 hours work for you.
\Y\ A caller logs on, and asks you if the games have been tested yet.
You explain that they're untested, so he asks if he can. You say yes, and 
the games work better than you think. You reward this user with an extra
30 mins.
\N\ When you wake up, you find that the computer, modem, monitor and
everything else has gone up in smoke, leaving you in debt up to your 
eyeballs.....

\Q\ You receive a voice call on the phone. Do you:
\A\ Quickly close the BBS and answer the phone
\A\ Ignore it.
\A\ Make a cup of coffee
\N\ When you closed the BBS, you discover that someone was online when
you did, and they ring back, promising that they will never call again.
\Y\ You hear the voice, but decide that it would take too much time to 
answer the phone and let them wait until you can call them back.
\N\ You make a cup of coffee that is the worse you've ever tasted, and think
to yourself that you should have answered the phone.

\Q\ A user wants to make a donation of a Texas Instruments computer. Do you:
\A\ Refuse the donation
\A\ Accept the donation
\A\ Ignore the user
\A\ Question why the user wishes to donate such an ancient machine
\N\ You offend the user, who says he will flame you on all the other BBS.
\N\ You accept the users donation, and find that most parts are missing.
\N\ After many messages and pages, the user gives up, saying that he/she had
an A3000 to donate as well.
\Y\ After much dicussion, you and the user decide that neither the user or
yourself will benefit from the donation.

\Q\ A user demands higher access. You decide to reward him/her as such:
\A\ Downgrade his/her security level
\A\ Upgrade his/her security level
\A\ Ignore the user
\N\ After downgrading the user's security level, he/she then accuses you of
being a hypocrite after he/she has made a donation.
(Should have taken the A3000!)
\N\ You leave a nasty letter addressed to the user for all to read, warning
him/her that an upgrade in security can only be done according to the rules.
\Y\ You ignore the user, and hear nothing more.

\Q\ You were busy typing out a letter to the taxman while the BBS is up,
and it crashes before you managed to save any data.
\A\ You decide to find out who was on and punish him/her
\A\ Reload the BBS and start again
\A\ Throw the keyboard out the window
\A\ Ring the taxman and plead for more time
\N\ The user WAS the taxman who called to tell you your $5000.00 cheque is 
in the mail, but after reading the nasty letter you left for him, he
cancelled it.
\N\ After reloading the BBS, the letter was lost forever, so you decide to
hang yourself. (The $5000.00 cheque comes the next day.....)
\N\ After throwing the keyboard out the window, the taxman arrives at your
house and thinks that this was an attempt on his life. You go to jail.
\Y\ The taxman listens to you, and agrees that you need some more time.

\Q\ A user uploads some pretty useless and crappy files
\A\ You delete the files
\A\ You delete the user
\A\ Leave the files there
\Y\ After deleting the files, you find out later that they were virus
infected, saving you work and time.
\N\ After deleting the user, the files that were uploaded contained viruses,
which infect every disk in your collection, making a weeks work for you.
\N\ You leave the files there, and find out over time that files are
suddenly being deleted and other files are corrupted, and by this time, the
BBS has been infected and you loose all the data.

\Q\ The phone company has sent you a bill for $2000.00. Do you:
\A\ Refuse to pay
\A\ Let the users know how much has to be paid
\A\ Ignore the bill
\N\ The line is cut off the next day, and the phone company will not put the
phone back on until it's paid.
\Y\ Some of your users decide to send in a donation to help with the phone
bill, so you reward them with an extra 30 mins online and an upgrade in their
security level.
\N\ After many months, the phone company sends a debt collector around to
get the money, and impounds all your computer equipment until paid.

\Q\ You Hard drive is giving you problems. What do you do?
\A\ Ignore it
\A\ Have a look at it
\A\ Buy a new Hard drive
\A\ Throw the Hard drive against the wall
\N\ The hard drive explodes in flames, leaving you to wonder if you should 
have fixed it.
\Y\ After opening the case, you find a loose screw which is all the problem
is.
\N\ Not a good thing to do, as the Hard drive seems to have fixed itself up,
and you end up a bankrupt.
\N\ This results in a neat little hole in the wall where the Hard drive is
imbedded.

\Q\ Your monitor is suffering from burn in (or burn out)
\A\ You buy a new monitor
\A\ You ignore the monitor
\A\ You swap with someone else
\A\ You use the TV
\N\ After buying your new monitor, it blows up after 1 hour's use,
leaving you stuck with the old monitor.
\Y\ You ignore the monitor, and find that the monitor is not suffering, but
you are suffering from fatigue after spending many late nights at the
keyboard.
\N\ After swapping with someone else, they accuse you of trying to rip them
off, as the monitor does not work.
\N\ After changing over to the TV, your eyesight declines, and sends you
blind.

\Q\ After spending many late nights at the keyboard your wife/girlfriend
threatens to leave you. You then think:
\A\ Let her
\A\ Plead for her to stay
\A\ Ignore her
\A\ Say "What did you say?"
\A\ Throw her on the bed and make make mad passionate love to her
\N\ She leaves you, along with all the money she gave you for your computer.
\N\ Your pleas fall on deaf ears, and she stomps out, vowing to send you
bankrupt with the divorce case.
\N\ She hearls a brass pot at you, and it lands right in the monitor.
\N\ She turns around and walks out.
\Y\ She is pleased that you have shown this deep love for her, but says that
if it continues, she will leave.

\Q\ You decide that you will expand the BBS. Do you:
\A\ Apply for a loan
\A\ Buy another Hard drive
\A\ Save some money
\N\ You approch the bank manager for a loan, but he laughes at you, saying
that the security needed for the loan wouldn't be reached.
\N\ You purchase another Hard drive, but it sends you bankrupt.
\Y\ You save enough money to purchase another Hard drive as well as another
computer to use.

\Q\ Your modem is not connecting to the incoming call. What do you do?
\A\ Get someone to have a look at it
\A\ Take it apart
\A\ Buy a new modem
\A\ Ignore it
\Y\ After taking it to a technian, it turns out to be only dust,
and he cleans it out.
\N\ After taking it apart, you discover that you didn't unplug it, therefore
giving yourself a 250,000 volt reminder to unplug it.
\N\ You like wasting money don't you? There's nothing wrong with the modem.
\N\ You ignore the modem, and it blows up into 3 pieces. The first piece ends
up in the ceiling, the 2nd out the window, and the last is embedded in your
head!

\Q\ Someone uploads a copyrighted game that has been hacked to the rims. 
What do you do?
\A\ Delete the file
\A\ Keep the file
\A\ Delete the file and the user
\A\ Hope no one finds out
\Y\ After deleting the file, you discover that other Sysops have been
prosecuted for having it in their library.
\N\ You are prosecuted for having a copyrighted game in your BBS and accused
of being the person who hacked it.
\N\ You delete the file and the user, but the user decides to say that you
were the one who hacked it.
\N\ All of a sudden, the police are very interested in your BBS, and you 
find that more and more of them are logging on your BBS.

\Q\ Your power supply has just melted. What do you do in panic?
\A\ Close the BBS
\A\ Leave the BBS open
\A\ Buy a new power supply
\A\ Leave everything alone
\W\ You manage to close the BBS in time, as the power supply just failed to
work at all.
\N\ You leave the BBS open, and the power supply decides that you won't have
the BBS open, and bursts into flames.
\N\ You like wasting money don't you? Why?
\N\ After going to bed that night, you discover that the computer, monitor,
modem, and Hard drive and decided to form into one mass of plastic.
\END\
